WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
In 1789, Jeremy Bentham wrote that
nature has placed us under 2 masters:

2
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.330
pain and pleasure.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:14.070
4 years earlier, Immanuel Kant said only
one thing is good without qualification:

4
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.620
a good will.

5
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.130
Bentham asks: what will happen?

6
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.590
Kant asks: what am I willing,
and could everyone will it?

7
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.470
So which fits a religious believer's
way of deciding what is right:

8
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.740
pleasure, or duty?

9
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:32.210
In this mission, you'll set
Bentham and Kant side by side,

10
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.530
row by row.

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.140
Then you'll explore how believers in
5 traditions make moral decisions.

12
00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: weigh up pleasure against
duty as a guide for religious believers.
